# Original fictional watershed-monitoring corpus for operational trials.
requirement OPS-MAINTAIN-001
title: Maintain deployed stations
statement:
  The monitoring service shall support diagnosis and controlled maintenance of deployed stations.
rationale:
  Remote stations require observable and bounded maintenance without routine site visits.
end requirement

requirement SYS-MAINTAIN-HEALTH-001
title: Report station health
statement:
  Each station shall report power, storage, sensor, processor, and communication health at least every five minutes.
decomposes: OPS-MAINTAIN-001
end requirement

requirement EDGE-HEALTH-001
title: Collect component health
statement:
  The station processor shall collect health observations from each configured station component.
decomposes: SYS-MAINTAIN-HEALTH-001
end requirement

requirement API-HEALTH-001
title: Present station health
statement:
  The maintenance interface shall present the latest health observations and their collection times for a requested station.
decomposes: SYS-MAINTAIN-HEALTH-001
end requirement

requirement SYS-MAINTAIN-CONFIG-001
title: Update station configuration
statement:
  The service shall apply an authorized configuration update atomically or retain the previous valid configuration.
decomposes: OPS-MAINTAIN-001
end requirement

requirement CONFIG-VERIFY-001
title: Verify configuration package
statement:
  The station processor shall verify the identity, integrity, and applicability of a configuration package before activation.
decomposes: SYS-MAINTAIN-CONFIG-001
end requirement

requirement CONFIG-ROLLBACK-001
title: Retain prior configuration
statement:
  The station processor shall restore the previous valid configuration when activation of an update fails.
decomposes: SYS-MAINTAIN-CONFIG-001
end requirement

requirement SYS-MAINTAIN-CALIBRATE-001
title: Manage sensor calibration
statement:
  The service shall apply and track sensor calibration and report upcoming calibration due dates.
decomposes: OPS-MAINTAIN-001
end requirement

requirement CAL-APPLY-001
title: Apply calibration data
statement:
  The station processor shall apply the active calibration data when converting each raw sensor sample.
decomposes: SYS-MAINTAIN-CALIBRATE-001
end requirement

requirement CAL-DUE-001
title: Report calibration due
statement:
  The maintenance interface shall identify sensors whose calibration is due within 30 days.
decomposes: SYS-MAINTAIN-CALIBRATE-001
end requirement
